  <title>Flat review</title>
  <p>
    Flat review lets you examine the visible contents of the active window independently of
    focus and the caret. Orca treats the window as a two-dimensional sequence of lines, items,
    and characters.
  </p>
  <p>
    Any flat review command starts reviewing the visible contents; off-screen content is not
    included. Orca refreshes the review context as the window, text, or caret changes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Flat Review preferences control whether the review location follows focus and caret changes.
    Using application navigation keys leaves flat review. You can also toggle flat review off
    and back on to rebuild the context.
  </p>
  <p>
    The home position is the beginning of the window's content; the end position is its last
    item. Bottom left is the start of the last line. Show flat review contents opens the entire
    review content in a text window.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-flat-review">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Flat Review</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Follow the focus and caret location</gui>: Controls when the
          flat review location moves to follow the focus or caret. Choices: Always,
          Automatically, Never.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Always</gui>: Flat review moves
              whenever the focus or caret location changes.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Automatically (default)</gui>: Orca decides when
              moving flat review to the focus or caret location is useful.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Never</gui>: Flat review stays where
              you last moved it.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Speak changes at review location</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca speaks content changes at the flat review location. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Display changes at review location</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca refreshes braille when content changes at the flat review location. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Restrict flat review to the current object</gui>: Controls whether
          flat review is limited to the current object instead of the whole window. Default:
          off.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
